# Pi agent

This repository was scaffolded with the Pi agent add-on. It lets the application run agentic flows by driving the [Pi coding agent](https://pi.dev) from Go, and adds two images that contain Pi.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["application code"] --> C["internal/piagent<br/>Go RPC client"]
    C -->|"JSON lines on stdin/stdout"| P["pi --mode rpc"]
    P --> M["model provider"]
    R["runtime image"] --> AG["agent image<br/>binary + Node + Pi"]
    S["sandbox image"] --> AS["agent-sandbox image<br/>toolchain + Node + Pi"]
```

## What was added

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `internal/piagent/` | A Go client for `pi --mode rpc`, standard library only |
{{- if eq .Stack "go-api-chi" }}
| `internal/httpapi/agent.go` | `POST /agent/prompt`, off unless `PI_AGENT_ENABLED=1` |
{{- else }}
| `cmd/agent.go` | The `agent` subcommand |
{{- end }}
| `Dockerfile.agent` | The `agent` and `agent-sandbox` image targets |
| `.config/mise/conf.d/pi.toml` | The `image:agent` and `image:agent:scan` tasks |

Pi's SDK is TypeScript-only. RPC mode is the interface Pi documents for other languages, so `internal/piagent` starts Pi as a child process and exchanges JSON records with it.

## Using the client

```go
client, err := piagent.Start(piagent.Options{Args: []string{"--model", "sonnet"}})
if err != nil {
	return err
}
defer func() { _ = client.Close() }()

result, err := client.Prompt(ctx, "Summarize the open TODOs in this repository", func(event piagent.Event) {
	fmt.Print(event.TextDelta()) // streams the answer as it arrives
})
```

- `Prompt` returns when Pi has no work left for the prompt. `result.Text` is the final assistant message.
- A `Client` keeps the conversation between prompts and runs one prompt at a time. Start one per conversation.
- Cancelling the context aborts the run.
- `Options.Args` takes any Pi flag, for example `--tools read,grep` to limit what the agent can do, or `--no-tools` for plain text generation.

{{ if eq .Stack "go-api-chi" -}}
## The HTTP endpoint

```sh
PI_AGENT_ENABLED=1 ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... go run ./cmd/api
curl -s localhost:8080/agent/prompt --json '{"prompt":"Say hello"}'
```

The route exists only when `PI_AGENT_ENABLED=1`. It has no authentication, and by default Pi can read and write files and run shell commands in its working directory, so put it behind your own authentication before exposing it. `PI_AGENT_ARGS` passes space-separated flags to Pi, for example `PI_AGENT_ARGS="--no-tools"`. Each request gets a fresh Pi process.
{{- else -}}
## The subcommand

```sh
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... go run . agent "Say hello"
go run . agent "Review this repository" -- --model sonnet --tools read,grep
```

Arguments after `--` are passed to Pi.
{{- end }}

## Images

| Target | Contents | Runs as | Use it for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `agent` | The application binary, Node, Pi, bash, git, ripgrep | UID 10001, in `/workspace` | Running the application where it needs Pi |
| `agent-sandbox` | Everything in `sandbox`, plus Node, Pi, ripgrep | UID 10001, in `/workspace` | Agents and jobs that work on this code with Pi |

| Command | What it does | Needs Docker |
|---|---|---|
| `mise run image:lint` | Lints `Dockerfile` and `Dockerfile.agent`; part of `mise run ci` | No |
| `mise run image:agent` | Builds `app:runtime` and `app:sandbox`, then `app:agent` and `app:agent-sandbox` on top of them | Yes |
| `mise run image:agent:scan` | Builds, then fails on fixable HIGH or CRITICAL findings in the agent image | Yes |

`Dockerfile.agent` reads the two base images from the local Docker image store, so build with the default `docker` build driver. The `runtime` and `sandbox` targets are unchanged: an image without Pi is still the default.

```sh
docker run --rm -e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY {{ if eq .Stack "go-api-chi" }}-e PI_AGENT_ENABLED=1 -p 8080:8080 app:agent{{ else }}app:agent agent "Say hello"{{ end }}
docker run --rm -it -e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -v "$PWD:/workspace" app:agent-sandbox pi
```

## Credentials and configuration

- Pi reads provider keys from the environment: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and others. Pass them at run time; nothing is baked into the images.
- Pi keeps settings and credentials under `~/.pi/agent` (`/home/agent/.pi/agent` in the images). Mount a volume there only if they should persist.
- Pi has no permission prompts. The container is the boundary: mount only the files, and pass only the credentials, a run needs.
- The images set `PI_SKIP_VERSION_CHECK=1` because Pi is pinned. Set `PI_TELEMETRY=0` to turn off Pi's install telemetry and provider attribution headers.

## Refreshing the pins

- `PI_VERSION` in `Dockerfile.agent` is an exact npm version. `npm view @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent version` prints the latest.
- The Node image is `tag@sha256:digest`. Pi needs Node 22.19 or newer. Replace the digest with the one this prints:

```sh
docker buildx imagetools inspect node:26.13.1-alpine3.24 --format '{{ "{{.Manifest.Digest}}" }}'
```
